# Project Wiki (engineering lessons)

When this repo contains `docs/wiki/SCHEMA.md`, treat that folder as the durable record of bugs fixed and invariants learned.

## Done gate (bug fixes)

After a **validated** non-trivial fix (repro known, root cause known, fix identified, verification passed):

1. Write `docs/wiki/incidents/<slug>.md` via the post-mortem skill shape.
2. Update `docs/wiki/index.md` and append `docs/wiki/log.md`.
3. Only then declare the bug-fix task done.

Skip typo / obvious one-liner fixes.

## Query first

On recurring-looking symptoms, read `docs/wiki/index.md` and matching incident/pattern pages before rediscovering from scratch.

## Boundaries

- Do not edit `docs/wiki/raw/` after it is committed (immutable evidence).
- This wiki is **not** a second memory system — claude-mem remains session memory SSOT.
- Do not auto-commit wiki pages unless the user asks.
